spans.s:
मारक f. ˚रिका killing, murdering (—˚);
 m. pestilence
(also r. ˚रिका), the god of death.

मा॑रण n. killing, slaughter, murder (w. प्राप् suffer
death);
 N. of a cert. magical ceremony & a mythical weapon.

मर्मज्ञ a. knowing the weak spots;
 i.g. knowing, clever,
deeply versed in or familiar with (—˚).

म॑र्य m. man, esp. young man, lover, suitor;
 pl. men,
servants, attendants.

मर्या॑दा f. limit, boundary, frontier;
 coast, shore;
 the
legal or moral bounds, order, law, rule, agreement, contract.

मर्यादिन् a. observing the boundaries;
 m. borderer,
neighbour.

मार्ग a. relating to game or deer. —n. (±मांस) game,
venison. m. track, way, path, road, passage;
 mode, manner, esp. right
manner, proper course;
 custom, use;
 title or head (j.), stile, diction.
मार्गेण & मार्गैस् through, along (—˚).

मार्गण a. asking, requiring (—˚). —m. beggar,
suppliant;
 arrow (abstr. ˚ता f.), n. searching, inquiring.

मार्जन f. ई wiping away, cleansing, washing;
 washerman
& woman. f. आ wiping out, washing;
 skin or sound of a drum;
 f. ई
cleansing, purifying, brush, broom;
 n. wiping out, sweeping, cleansing,
effacing.

मार्जाली॑य a. fond of washing (E. of Śiva);
 m. (scil.
धि॑ष्ण्य) a heap of earth to the right of the Vedi ((r.))

मार्जित a. cleaned, polished, smeared with (instr.);
 wiped
off, removed, destroyed.
